Chat page QA (#133): screen-reader names on the chat page, in Arabic and matching what is on screen.
- Toast region: Radix's default label «Notifications (F8)» was announced in English on every page; it now uses the
  interface language (com_efaiw_notifications_region, the {hotkey} placeholder is Radix's own).
- Model button: its accessible name was always «اختر نموذجًا» while it shows «بصير لايت» (WCAG 2.5.3 Label in Name,
  level A: a voice-control user saying the visible name could not reach it). The name now starts with the visible
  model name and keeps the action: «بصير لايت، اختر نموذجًا». With nothing selected it stays «اختر نموذجًا».
- History item: a chat without a generated title showed «دردشة جديدة» but was announced as «محادثة New Chat» (the
  stored default title); the accessible name now uses the displayed title.

